description: Merged PR branches stay on origin: as of 2026-11-17 there were 67 of them, 32 from your PRs and 35 from ours. We just deleted our 35, each merged at its current head and unused as a base by any open PR.
 
 Proposal: turn on "Automatically delete head branches" in the repo settings, so GitHub deletes a PR's branch when it merges. What it changes:
 
 - It applies to every PR, yours included. A stack still works: GitHub retargets the child PR to the merged PR's base before deleting the branch.
 - A deleted branch can be restored from the PR page.
 
 Your 32 merged branches (`llvm-parity-1-apps` through `llvm-parity-6-leaves-design`, `checks-sideband`, and the rest) are yours to keep or delete; we haven't touched them.
 
 If you're fine with it, reply here and we'll flip the setting.
